# Warp is cast from the hand only (CR 702.185a: "You may cast this card from your hand for its warp cost"). Bot1 warps
# Quantum Riddler for {1}{U} on turn 1 (Island, Mox Sapphire); at the end step it is exiled, and its owner may cast it
# from exile on a later turn. On turn 7 Bot1 has five mana up (four Islands and the Mox), enough for the warp cost, but
# the card is in exile, so warp is not offered (refused); it is cast for its mana cost {3}{U}{U} instead (the positive
# control). Not warped this time, it is not exiled at that turn's end step: it is still on the battlefield on turn 8.

